This program simulates two scheduling algorithms, First Come First Served (FCFS) and Shortest Job First (SJF), on the same set of processes. For FCFS, it insertion-sorts the processes by arrival time and runs each one to completion in that order, moving the clock forward over any idle gap when nothing has arrived yet. For SJF, it first insertion-sorts by burst time. Then, at each scheduling point, it picks the shortest job that has already arrived, or jumps the clock to the next arrival if none has, and runs that job to completion. For every process it records waiting time and turnaround time, then prints a chart with idle periods marked and the average of each metric.
